# The eight wanderer roles: one topic each, on top of their built verbs (their special, Share some
# food, Rob). They speak for themselves, in the first person. No pronouns for them in our lines.

conv wanderer.trader.prices
for wanderer:trader
topic "What's selling these days?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say Batteries, always. Salt, since the shop in {here} went. Boots in your size, never. People pay for warmth and light before they pay for food, which surprised me.
  say Jewellery sells to the Red Hand. Don't ask me what they do with it. They weigh it on a kitchen scale and write it in a book.
  > @cheap Anything going cheap? -> cheap
  > @other Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node cheap
  say Advice. Here's some, free: never buy a tin that's been opened and closed again. And never sell your boots. Everything else you can buy back. Not boots.
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.doctor.work
for wanderer:doctor
topic "How's the work going, Doctor?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say Same as the old job. People come in hurt, I fix what I can, and I write down what I can't. I did twelve-hour shifts at the hospital. Now it's one long shift with walking in it.
  say The difference is nobody pays the electricity bill. Including me. I've stitched a man up by a car's headlights twice this week.
  > @shop Let's compare what we're carrying. -> shop   if bg:doctor,nurse
  > @worst What's the worst of it? -> worst
  > @other2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node shop
  say Show me yours. Gauze, good. That antiseptic is half water, whoever sold it to you. The Red Hand cut everything, even the stuff you put on wounds.
  say Clean a bite first, then argue about it. The first minutes are the ones that count. After that you're cleaning it for your own peace of mind.
  do learn:doctor.golden_window
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node worst
  say The bites people don't mention until the fever's up. By then I'm a witness, not a doctor. I sit with them, and I write down the time.
  say Tell someone early. Anyone. A Haven house, the lab, me. It's the only advice I've given in eleven days that's ever worked.
  > @back3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.scavenger.where
for wanderer:scavenger
topic "Where have you been lately?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say Everywhere twice and nowhere I'd go a third time. The empty villages, the farms, the petrol stations on the ring road. {here} has a chemist's with the shutters down.
  say Down isn't locked. Down is just down.
  > @true Is that true, about the chemist's? -> honest | shrug   check persuade none 2 bg:police,elder
  > @other3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node honest
  say Mostly. The shutters are down because something leans on them from inside. I heard it shift when I knocked. I didn't stop to ask what.
  do learn:scav.chemist
  > @back4 Good to know. One more thing. -> hub

node shrug
  say True enough to sell. That's the only kind of true I can afford out here. You want the other kind, you'll have to pay for it like everybody else.
  > @back5 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.deserter.why
for wanderer:deserter
topic "Why did you leave Bastion?"
prio world
voice plain

node start
  say I didn't leave. On paper I'm dead. Killed in action, body not recovered. My name's still up on their board, with a date that isn't true.
  say They'll read it at the roll tonight, and the whole post will answer here for me, all together. That's the worst part. They mean it.
  > @why2 What made you go? -> why | silent   check persuade none 2 bg:soldier,police
  > @back Could you ever go back? -> back
  > @other4 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node why
  say Orders came that nobody read out loud. The sergeant read them alone, then burnt them in the stove. I'd read them first, over the radio man's shoulder.
  say I won't say what they said. I left because I'd have done it. I'd have done it and signed for it, and I'd have slept fine. That's what scared me.
  do learn:bastion.orders_rumour
  > @back6 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node silent
  say Because I wanted to live more than I wanted to be counted. Leave it there. Please. I've said it to nobody else, and I'd like to keep it that way.
  > @back7 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node back
  say If I walked in, they'd rub out the killed in action. Not the man. Then they'd deal with me for walking, properly signed for, and the board would get it right this time.
  > @back8 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.preacher.bells
for wanderer:preacher
topic "Tell me about the bells."
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say I took them down from the church at the crossroads on Day 4, after the priest opened the doors to everyone and somebody had to keep time while he did.
  say I ring them so the living know someone's still keeping the hours. The sick hear them too. I've asked the Lord which matters more. He's been quiet on it.
  > @danger They draw the sick into town. -> danger
  > @other5 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node danger
  say They do. That's why I ring and walk on, and never twice in one place. You can ask me to stop for a while. I'll listen. I've been wrong before.
  > @back9 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.courier.post
for wanderer:courier
topic "What's in the bag?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say Letters. People still write them, on whatever they've got: the backs of calendars, wallpaper, a cereal box once. Half the addresses are houses that aren't there any more.
  say I deliver those to the nearest house that is. Somebody reads them out at supper. It helps, somehow. People like to hear that somebody wrote.
  > @read Do you ever read them? -> read
  > @last Who wrote the last one you carried? -> last
  > @other6 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node read
  say Never. The day I start reading them is the day I start choosing which ones to lose. I carry them all the same, good news and bad, sealed.
  > @back10 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node last
  say A man at a Bastion post, to his wife on the other side of the line. I can't deliver it. I told him so. He said carry it anyway, so somebody's carrying it.
  say It's at the bottom of the bag. It's the only one I'll never put down. When the line opens, that's the first door I knock on.
  > @back12 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv wanderer.mechanic.cars
for wanderer:mechanic
topic "What still runs, these days?"
prio flavour
voice plain

node start
  say Anything with a carburettor and an owner who's not coming back for it. Fuel's the problem, not the cars. Every garage forecourt in the Zone ran dry on Day 2.
  say The Red Hand has most of the diesel now. Ask them nicely, pay what they ask, and then check your pockets.
  > @fix Teach me a trick I don't know. -> fix   if bg:mechanic
  > @other7 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node fix
  say You know the tricks. Here's one you don't: the Bastion trucks use a different fuel cap from the civvy ones. Take a spare off a wreck and keep it in your bag.
  do learn:mechanic.bastion_caps
  > @back11 Let me ask you something else. -> hub
